{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.MassIdentityExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.MassIdentityExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassIdentity.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassIdentity.exists","kind":"theorem","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-exists.lean#L20-L34","doc":"**Well-definedness of the inertial mass identity.**\n\nFor every normed commutative ring `R` and closed cycle morphism\non a Frobenius-Hopf object, the inertial mass\n`scalarMass` / `massComposite` evaluates to an element of `R` —\ni.e. the definitions from `QOU.MassIdentity` are well-typed on\nvalid input.  This records the claim at the type level via a\n`Nonempty R` witness (trivial for non-trivial `R`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:mass-identity-exists","label":"prop:mass-identity-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}